The Legend of Zelda has a plethora of  hidden mechanics and concepts that are  useful to know as you explore it's  hostile yet mysterious world to increase  your chances of survival we've compiled  seven handy tips you might not know be  weary there are potential spoilers ahead  if you enjoy this video like it and  subscribe to our YouTube channel for  more features on breath of the wild and  be sure to watch our previous videos on  all the things I wish I knew before I  started you can temporarily expand your  horse's stamina when you cook Endora  carrots into a dish it creates food that  temporarily increases your stamina but  you're not the only one who can benefit  from this tasty veggie give a raw one to  a horse and their stamina temporarily  increases by three your horse maintains  this stamina boost just as long as you  don't spur through it so don't push your  trusty steed too hard you can find  indoor carrots in the fair and  grasslands and Hyrule Ridge but you're  guaranteed to find some around melania  spring or by the trees that surround the  great fairy fountain in Kakariko village  treasure chest indicator there are  always hidden treasure chests to find in  the myriad shrines you visit if you're a  completionist the thought of not  uncovering all of them probably drives  you crazy thankfully the game has a way  of telling you when you've collected  everything in a shrine simply highlight  a shrine on the map and if it has a  treasure chest beside its name and that  means you've uncovered all of its secret  chests if it doesn't have this indicator  then you'd best go back and see what you  missed the Master Sword beam much like  past Zelda games breadth of the wilds  Master Sword also has a beam attack you  can use to fire at enemies from a  distance and as you'd expect you need to  be at full health to use it to use the  sword beam simply hold the R button to  aim the master sword and then release it  to fire a disc of energy the sword beam  is a useful Albia tweak attack that you  can spam quite often before the Master  Sword runs out of energy plus it's a  great way to hunt all those pesky  woodland critters  use the proper tools for the job  while you're out gathering essential  resources such as wood and ore from the  environment you might think that using  your weapons or bombs is the best way to  obtain them these are perfectly viable  techniques to gather resources but they  actually serve to your detriment to  optimize wood gathering use of wood  cutters axe it can chop down a tree in  two strikes and if you use a double axe  you can down a tree with a single swing  to find these weapons you need only  travel to any stable they'll likely be  hedged into a tree stump or leaning  against a wall if you're still using  bombs to break open rocks you've got to  change your ways after all I'm sure  you're frustrated when this constantly  happens to you there are tools available  that make gathering or way easier the  boulder breaker for instance can break  open rocks with a single heavy blow but  the drill shaft is far more efficient  requiring a single jab to break open  rocks quickly and easily you can find  both of these weapons lying around the  Eldon canyons you can get a Hylian  Shield the classic Hylian Shield appears  in breath of the wild and it's pretty  much the strongest shield in the game  [Music]  but where is it  Hyrule Castle oh man okay if you possess  the courage to go alone and are well  equipped with Hart's equipment and  weapons head to the southwest section of  the castle and look across the moat to  see a minecart rail use your cry Onis  rune to cross the moat and head into the  right tunnel follow it until you find a  minecart then hop in and use your stasis  room to propel the cart back where you  came falling the rails to the other  tunnel entrance continue through the  cave until you find this cracked wall  blow it up with a bomb  enter through the opening in its wake  and make a left to find a prison lock up  continue to the back until you see two  torches blow up the broken stone wall  between them you'll notice Elizabeth and  a mob limb but in order to open the cell  door to get to them you'll need to use  an arrow to shoot the switch through the  cell bars once you kill both of them  make a left and then a right into the  room filled with bones these bones then  assemble into a stall knocks mini-boss  defeated and the shield is yours  [Music]  it's important to note that if you  happen to lose or break the Hylian  Shield finish the from the ground up  side quest so you can buy it back from  grata in Tarrytown cooked hearty foods  offer full heart recovery and then some  if you're looking to minimize the grind  for health cook foods that have the word  Hardy in its name cooking these items  heal your hearts fully while adding a  fair number of temporary hearts to your  health a great place to farm for hearty  foods is the lush brownness forest in  the Ferren region which you can get to  if you head north  affarin tower the area's trees are  loaded with upwards of 15 hardy durians  this is a big deal since a cooked hearty  durian will heal you fully and grant you  in extra for hearts and if you cook  three that's 12 extra hearts and if you  get five we're talking 20 extra hearts  added to your health i'm telling you you  can't get more hearts anywhere else  consider bringing an axe to speed up the  process as it rains quite often in this  area making it hard to climb up trees  regardless once you've ransacked this  hot spot just come back after every  Blood Moon to find it restocked you can  mount a Lionel if you've completed the  zora portion of your main quest then  chances are you'll know about the  devastating power of Lionel's  these scents are like beings will stop  at nothing to eliminate you making  persistent use of both their melee  weapon and bow to cause you all sorts of  grief but it's possible to humiliate  these terrifying foes by stunning and  mounting them before you confront a line  although it's recommended that you grab  the stasis room upgrade from pura when  you're ready to fight one make sure to  maintain your distance you stasis when  it's about to charge at you once frozen  quickly shoot a bomb or fire arrow at  its head to stun it when it's down  quickly mount them and toss in a few  swipes at their neck  rinse and repeat this process until you  defeat it at times mounting a Lionel  doesn't seem worth it seeing as it's  possible to inflict the same amount of  damage when you're simply going toe to  toe with it but gosh is it fulfilling to  watch these jerks flail helplessly for  once in their lives what other cool and  useful mechanics have you found let us  know in the comments below and for more  coverage on the Legend of Zelda breath  of the wild be sure to subscribe to our  YouTube channel  [Music]
 

